  "resolution": [
    "MCP internal target/removal guards compare actual edits with a non-secret baseline; unchanged selections and successful explicit saves do not prompt. Confirmation is revoked after owner, visibility, readiness or configuration version changes.",
    "Remote sharing guards only the replaced remote editor, keeps canceled edits and missing-target drafts visible with mutations disabled, and revokes pending selection when directory identity changes. Later recipient edits are not marked saved by earlier acknowledgements.",
    "Provider model-directory editors are keyed by provider identity rather than every registry revision. Refreshes keep unsaved rows/manual input and reset capability consent; old action scopes cannot publish or clear state. Provider changes/removal guard child drafts; profile restore remains disabled until edits are saved/discarded. Explicit catalog discard is available; exact saved edits do not trigger redundant prompts.",
    "Worktree retirement uses a concise action label while retaining the detailed warning, clean-only semantics and exact-version checkbox."
  ],
